        <div class="col-sm-4">
          <img alt="Synapse Test State Optimizer" src="/images/samplecube2.png"
            class="hidden-xs centerImg leftImgAlignH1-H3" style="margin-top: 50px; max-height: 250px">
          <img alt="Synapse Test State Optimizer Stage 2" src="/images/samplecube3.png"
            class="centerImg leftImgAlignH1-H3" style="max-width: 250px">
          <img alt="Synapse Test State Optimizer Final" src="/images/samplecube.png"
            class="hidden-xs centerImg leftImgAlignH1-H3" style="max-width: 250px">
        </div>
        <div style="position: relative; z-index: 1;" class="col-xs-12 col-sm-7">
          <h2>Unleash State Machine Speed</h2>
          <p class="main">
            Under the surface of the graphical programming environment is a fundamentally different interaction of
            software and hardware. Test programs are compiled into a dedicated, run-time state machine on FPGAs that
            drive the instrumentation and signal processing in real time. This produces faster tests, consistent
            measurements, and enables a powerful feature never before possible in an ATE system - intelligent test
            optimization. Built into the compiler is Synapse, a test state optimizer that guarantees the most
            efficient
            program execution on any tester configuration. </p>
          <ul style="padding-right: 40px;">
            <li>
              <img alt="Typical Test Flow (time)" src="/images/synapse_flow1.jpg"
                style="margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 5px; max-width: 100%">
              Typical test programs are designed with an execution order that follows the programmer’s code
              organization. While conventional, this can have unintended inefficiencies — redundant program calls,
              unnecessary instrument settings, and repeated test states. Code optimization and reuse across different
              devices requirements and tester configurations can quickly become unmanageable.
            </li>
            <li>
              <img alt="Synapse Test State Optimizer (Optimized Time)" src="/images/synapse_flow2.jpg"
                style="margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 5px; max-width: 100%">
              Synapse optimizes test execution using an advanced state analysis of measurement setup and program flow.
              This removes superfluous test states, groups similar types, executes repeated measurement setups in
              parallel, and organizes the overall test flow to reduce processing and execution overhead.
            </li>
            <li><img alt="Synapse Test State Optimizer (Fastest Test Time)" src="/images/synapse_flow3.jpg"
                style="margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 5px; max-width: 100%">
              The result is a test program that is twice as fast (Typical test time improvement) and guarantees the
              most efficient execution on any Cassini instrument and tester configuration. With full user control over
              where and how Synapse optimizes the test program, the focus can be put back on test and measurement
              design.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <a title="Learn about what makes RI Fastest" href="/fastest.html">
            Learn More &raquo;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- .row -->
